  "limitations": [
    "RSS is a process-level proxy from a continuously drained reader; it does not prove the hidden cdpkit subscriber queue is bounded",
    "ack latency values are receive-to-ack-completion proxies, not wire-enqueue timestamps",
    "candidate-contract trace digest: sha256:6c6be028c511d4d8c28cbecec368a7d4f09e0d87612741d02ac19a8663964d54",
    "cdpkit exposes named event params through an unbounded subscriber; wildcard/full-envelope receive and queue-depth introspection are unavailable"
  ],
  "rejected_alternatives": [
    "chromey 2.52.0 was not tested because cdpkit passed every unchanged gate; revisit it only after a demonstrated cdpkit lifecycle, ordering, or sustained-capture failure",
    "an owned Tokio/tokio-tungstenite transport was not selected because cdpkit preserved the required raw command and named-event boundary without a fork"
  ],
  "rationale": "Exact cdpkit 0.4.0 passed all 13 unchanged gates on both Linux and macOS; the named-event-params limitation and unbounded subscriber-depth limitation remain explicit, so the production adapter must preserve Krometrail-owned reconnect, bounded handoff, and backpressure policy behind a replaceable boundary."
}